WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:26.820
I can't afford to lose either.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.330
There's a battle that I want to fight.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.140
I won't give up!

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.870
I activate a spell card!

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.980
Giant Trunade!

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.550
What?

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:51.080
I can't leave this card in the graveyard.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.550
I have no regrets!

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:55.990
Bring it, Jonouchi!

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.160
Panther Warrior attacks!

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.150
I'll treasure this card!

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.280
You better!

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.300
I'll win next time!

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.160
I'll be stronger too!

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:33.460
Curse of the Mask
Skyscraper Duel

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.330
I did it, Shizuka!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.700
I made the tournament finals!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.710
Wow!  Congrats, big brother!

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:43.450
Well, I still have a lot to do.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.550
But you defeated strong duelists, right?

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.880
You're incredible!

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:50.550
You think?

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.820
Your words make me happy.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.600
I have six Puzzle Cards.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.860
I might have grown as a duelist.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.430
Big brother...

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.760
What is it?

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.130
Can I come see you in the tournament finals?

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.260
But you haven't removed your bandages yet.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.300
No, but the doctor said I could remove them soon.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:22.500
Besides, I promised that the first thing I'll see is you dueling.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:23.950
Yeah.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.120
Okay, we'll pick you up because it's dangerous to travel alone.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.900
Make sure to get the doctor's permission.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.060
Okay.  Thank you, big brother.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:35.990
Woohoo!

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:42.570
Don't throw my cell phone!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.350
Shizuka will watch me duel in the finals!

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.970
What about her eyes?

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.980
She's now allowed to remove her bandages.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.770
That's great news!

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.980
I want to go pick her up, but I have the finals...

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.980
But I can't let her travel alone...

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.900
You can count on me!

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.530
Leave her to me!

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:11.960
Hey, Honda!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.200
Sheesh...

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:17.480
Yugi, I've fulfilled our promise.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:18.620
Wait for me.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.180
Bakura!

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.160
Bakura!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.860
What happened?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.050
Are you okay?

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.580
You're badly hurt!

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.360
I think someone attacked him.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.900
Thank goodness.  Are you his friends?

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.200
Who would do such a thing?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.600
Jonouchi...

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.930
Bakura, what happened?

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.200
I don't know.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.360
I don't remember.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.710
I gave him first aid, but he needs to go to the hospital.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.710
Yeah.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.310
Thank you.  We'll take care of him.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.760
Jonouchi, give me a hand.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.240
Right.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.080
Leave Bakura to me.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.380
Thanks, Gramps.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.280
You sure he's inside?

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:25.620
Yeah.  My Satellite Search System detected that your friend was dueling here.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:33.230
I can't understand why you're so focused on finding an amateur.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.530
Thank you, umm...

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.920
What's your name?

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.140
I'm Namu.  Nice to meet you.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.240
I'm Jonouchi.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.840
Anzu.  Thank you for everything.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.760
I only did what I had to do.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.430
You're a duelist too?

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.800
Yes.  But I'm not that good.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:02.240
Don't ask me to duel you.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.910
I've already made it through the prelims.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.120
Wow!  You must be skilled!

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.550
I should ask you for advice.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.640
Go ahead.  Any time.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.820
I feel like we're friends already.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.710
Yeah, we're friends!

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:21.970
Let's go, Namu.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.000
Okay.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.510
Friends...

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.650
Master Marik.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:38.440
We've confirmed that Kaiba has Obelisk the Tormentor.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.130
I see.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:46.040
How is Kaiba able to control Obelisk?

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.390
Not everyone can use God Cards.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.800
They choose their owners.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:58.000
That question will be irrelevant if you get Obelisk the Tormentor back.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:06.200
True.  Can you retrieve Obelisk the Tormentor and Yugi's Slifer the Sky Dragon?

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:09.200
Of course.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.410
Because we're using the deck you created that seals away the Gods.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.800
Fine.  You're up.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.750
But don't kill him quickly.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.280
The Pharaoh must suffer.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:26.480
He must experience the pain that my family went through.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.330
Then I'll finish him.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.300
It's not that I don't trust them.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.230
I'm just very careful.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.240
Just in case, I'll use these two...

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.970
Hey, Jonouchi.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.340
What's up?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:50.110
Sorry to be pushy, but can you give me some dueling advice now?

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.830
Sure!

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.420
I want to win at least once in Battle City.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.530
You still have chance.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.860
With my advice, you might make the finals!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.160
Jonouchi!  Anzu!

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:08.260
Where are you?

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.270
Big talk.  Can you back it up?

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:12.530
Leave it to me!

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.470
Jonouchi!

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.650
Jonouchi!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.160
What are you doing?

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.070
You must be Ghouls!

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.700
You're after Jonouchi's rare cards!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.890
Anzu!  Jonouchi!  Run!

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.460
Namu!

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.620
Stop it!

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.530
Don't hurt my friend!

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:50.000
This is also payback for your sneak attack the other night!

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:52.090
How's that!

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.140
Anzu!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.320
Jonouchi...

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.760
How dirty!  Let Anzu go!

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.170
Jonouchi!  Namu!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.540
Hello?  Anzu?

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:23.900
Yugi...

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.900
Hello?  Hello?

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.110
Yugi, save me!

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:33.770
Anzu?

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.320
Anzu!

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:43.060
I can easily get the God Card back if I involve your friends.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:48.370
The Ghouls' Rare Hunters have been watching your friends all this time.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.700
I can use them anytime I want.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:56.710
You better go to your friends before something tragic happens to them.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.080
Marik!

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:06.380
Do the Ghouls have my friends?

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.180
Anzu's cell phone isn't picking up.

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.820
The Ghouls may have taken her.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.760
Don't worry, Yugi.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.260
I told Mokuba to find their location.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.700
He'll find them soon.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.640
What a strange situation.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:35.180
I'm walking side-by-side with my eternal enemy.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:41.980
Even though I want to defeat you right here, right now.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:47.960
Kaiba, I can only think about my friends for now.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:52.890
Big brother!

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.060
Mokuba.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:01.900
It's weird.  Headquarters can't find Jonouchi's location.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:06.760
Even though they locked on to his Duel Disk during his last duel.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.710
I'll go back to HQ and check myself.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.230
Understood.  Thanks, Mokuba.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.650
We don't know where the amateur is.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:21.000
Even though Kaiba Corporation's satellite system is perfect.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.240
You're...

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:55.160
What's up?  You look very happy today.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:59.310
My brother made it to the Battle City Finals.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:01.440
Really?  That's incredible!

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:06.300
Yes.  And I decided to go see him in the finals.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:10.100
You're ready to remove your bandages?

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:16.040
If I meet my brother, I'll have the courage.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:25.950
They're here.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:29.800
Lead them to the special duel arena.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.000
Leave it to me.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.140
A Ghoul?

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.740
Look at that!

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.570
That's...

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:01.970
Mokuba!

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.150
Mokuba!

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:34.190
Damn Ghouls!

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:40.270
I'll punish you if you leave even a single scratch on Mokuba!

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:44.600
I'll use all of Kaiba Corporation's resources to crush you!

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.360
How scary.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.540
If you try to hurt us, your cute brother will be...

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:53.130
You punk!

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.360
We'll wait for you on top of that skyscraper.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:02.220
You know what happens if you don't show up.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.420
Mokuba!

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.530
You're coming too, Yugi.

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:17.400
Or we'll dispose of your friends.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:18.570
What?

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:22.620
You took them?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.640
I'll be waiting.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:29.310
Come quickly to the duel arena of death!

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.000
Yugi, we have to go.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:33.580
Yeah.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.250
I'll crush them with all my might!

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:39.280
But don't get the wrong idea.

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:45.110
I'm only doing this for Mokuba.  You're doing this for your friends.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.420
I know.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.790
Thanks for coming.

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:17.100
We haven't introduced ourselves.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:21.160
We're Ghouls's assassins.  I'm Mask of Light.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:24.600
I'm Mask of Darkness.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:29.540
We formed this tag team specifically to hunt for God Cards.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.400
I'll explain the rules.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.260
It's a two-on-two tag duel.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:46.560
If you lose all your life points, you leave the game.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.590
The team that defeats both opponents wins.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.450
But be careful.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:55.030
"Leaving the game" means you die.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:16:00.720
We're standing on the roof of a 130-meter building.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:04.320
Beneath the glass, it's open all the way down to the first floor.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:16.980
This invisible sheet of glass is keeping us alive.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:23.360
There are explosives on each of the four sections where we're standing.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:29.960
When your life counter reaches 0, the explosive detonates.

00:16:32.960 --> 00:16:38.240
The glass beneath your feet will shatter, and you will fall.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:45.000
I call this "The Fall and Die Expolosive Tag Match!"

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.160
How fun!

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:52.020
You're too scared to speak.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.400
Is that all you want to say?

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:57.420
Do you guarantee that Mokuba is safe?

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:00.960
Yeah.  Until this duel ends.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:06.400
In the unlikely event that you win, we'll return him to you.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:10.710
It seems you Ghouls still have a shred of pride left.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:15.410
I'll take you on with my deck full of anger!

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:25.100
You think you can defeat us?

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:32.160
My Mask Card Deck seals away all abilities, so even the God Cards can't beat it.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:37.600
There's no way you can defeat the Light and Darkness tag team.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.800
Here we go!  Duel!

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.460
I go first.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:53.960
In a tag duel, each team alternate turns, one player at a time.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:58.030
I draw a card.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:03.000
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.670
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:08.020
He set his cards...

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.830
I draw!

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:12.900
My card is...

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:17.970
Beta The Magnet Warrior in defense position.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.510
I end my turn.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.890
No player can attack on their first turn.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:27.650
I wonder what strategy they'll use.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.320
My turn.

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:33.170
Shining Abyss in defense position!

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.620
Since my partner summoned a monster...

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.560
A spell card?

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:43.560
The spell card Mask of Brutality!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:49.940
That mask card powers up my monster!

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:09.220
What?  He has a monster with over 2000 attack points on the first turn!

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:17.210
Unfortunately, I have to pay 1000 life points during my Standby Phases to keep this monster.

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.270
Don't worry, partner.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:23.850
I play the Continuous Spell Masked Doll.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:33.350
This doll absorbs all curses from masks.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:39.760
So Mask of Brutality's maintenance cost is negated.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.390
That's great, partner.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:43.800
See that?

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:46.330
This is our combination play style.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:52.650
I see.  Their tag duel strategy relies on teamwork.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.550
Lame.

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:58.940
Teamwork is a hindrance during battle.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:00.270
Kaiba...

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:04.800
Yugi, you're only here to commemorate my victory.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:09.650
I'll crush these lame Ghouls on my own.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.750
Here I go!  My turn!

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.720
I set a card!

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:22.330
And I summon the killer Beast-Warrior, Vorse Raider!

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:30.000
I place it in attack position and end my turn.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.020
Attack position?

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:37.880
He's inviting them to attack so that he can counter with a set card.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:42.100
I have a strong Level 6 monster in my hand.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:47.340
I'll tribute Vorse Raider to summon it next turn.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:54.660
He's planning to tribute his monster and summon a higher Level monster next turn.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.330
But it won't go as planned.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:05.500
They're confident because they have a strategy for this tag duel.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.380
But Kaiba wants to fight alone.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:24.160
Under these circumstances, how will I be able to save my friends?

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:42.240
Mokuba, they caught you too?

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:47.310
The Ghouls locked us inside this warehouse.  What are they planning to do?

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:52.880
Yugi and Kaiba are having trouble against the masked Rare Hunters' teamwork.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:57.690
They're no longer allowed to Tribute Summon, so they can't summon high Level monsters.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:22:01.930
Yugi wants to work together with Kaiba, but does Kaiba?

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:04.940
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
God Cards Sealed Away

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:06.400
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:25.770
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:31.140
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:40.790
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:52.300
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:55.190 --> 00:22:59.830
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:05.110
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.660 --> 00:23:10.210
Will never change

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:15.480
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:16.110 --> 00:23:20.690
To be who I am

00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:25.930
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:30.630
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:33.530
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:40.670
From now until forever...
